WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.585 --> 00:00:17.872
The were coming from the bandstand.

2
00:00:19.973 --> 00:00:22.535
Daisy saw a young man playing a saxophone.

3
00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:25.516
"Oh! That's my clarinet teacher."

4
00:00:26.237 --> 00:00:26.997
Grace waved.

5
00:00:27.017 --> 00:00:28.818
"Hi, Riley!"

6
00:00:28.838 --> 00:00:30.679
"Oh, hey, Grace!"

7
00:00:31.319 --> 00:00:32.360
Riley waved back.

8
00:00:32.948 --> 00:00:34.128
"My band is about to play.

9
00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:37.009
I hope you'll stay and listen."

10
00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:41.270
"Sure!" Grace introduced Daisy and Kaleem.

11
00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:43.431
"Nice to meet you."

12
00:00:43.991 --> 00:00:45.772
Riley hopped down from the stage.

13
00:00:45.792 --> 00:00:48.072
"And who's this?"

14
00:00:48.713 --> 00:00:49.993
He rubbed Scamp's head.

15
00:00:50.013 --> 00:00:52.514
"My dog, Scamp," Grace said.

16
00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:57.115
"I wish my wife wasn't afraid of dogs," Riley said.

17
00:00:57.135 --> 00:01:00.776
"We live out in the country with lots of space for a dog to play."

18
00:01:02.044 --> 00:01:03.565
One of his bandmates heard him.

19
00:01:04.186 --> 00:01:05.286
"I'm glad you live there.

20
00:01:06.187 --> 00:01:09.349
We can rehearse as loudly as we want without bothering anybody."

21
00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:11.591
Riley chuckled.

22
00:01:11.611 --> 00:01:14.172
"That's Spike.

23
00:01:14.452 --> 00:01:16.634
She plays guitar and sings some of our songs.

24
00:01:17.034 --> 00:01:17.775
I sing the rest."

25
00:01:18.515 --> 00:01:19.836
He kept petting Scamp.

26
00:01:19.856 --> 00:01:23.178
"I've never had a dog, but I had a parrot as a teenager.

27
00:01:23.759 --> 00:01:24.879
He was my muse."

28
00:01:24.899 --> 00:01:27.601
"What's a muse?"

29
00:01:28.001 --> 00:01:28.802
Daisy asked.

30
00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:31.424
"It's someone who inspires an artist."

31
00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:32.780
Riley grinned.

32
00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:36.782
"That bird inspired me to start writing songs.

33
00:01:37.482 --> 00:01:38.343
I still miss him.

34
00:01:39.183 --> 00:01:41.244
I had to find him a new home when I went to college.

35
00:01:42.164 --> 00:01:43.765
He was too noisy to live in a dorm."

36
00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:50.668
Soon Riley's band began to play.

37
00:01:52.368 --> 00:01:54.269
Kaleem bopped his head to the beat.

38
00:01:54.289 --> 00:01:55.870
"They're good!"

39
00:01:58.071 --> 00:02:00.572
Riley grabbed the microphone and started singing.

40
00:02:02.604 --> 00:02:06.586
Just as he hit a high note, another sound drowned him out.

41
00:02:07.307 --> 00:02:10.589
Yooowl! "What's that?"

42
00:02:10.889 --> 00:02:11.489
Grace said.

43
00:02:11.509 --> 00:02:14.511
"It sounds like a cat," Daisy said.

44
00:02:14.531 --> 00:02:17.373
"And now lots of dogs are barking!"

45
00:02:17.393 --> 00:02:19.694
"Where's the cat?"

46
00:02:20.234 --> 00:02:22.195
Scamp barked, joining the chorus.

47
00:02:26.198 --> 00:02:27.799
The kids ran to the shelter booth.

48
00:02:28.499 --> 00:02:29.720
All the dogs were barking.

49
00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:36.185
Inside the cat tent, a beautiful Siamese cat was yowling loudly.

50
00:02:36.205 --> 00:02:40.246
"What's wrong, kitty?"

51
00:02:40.526 --> 00:02:41.307
Daisy asked.

52
00:02:42.407 --> 00:02:44.167
The shelter manager came over.

53
00:02:45.548 --> 00:02:47.308
Her nametag read Joan.

54
00:02:47.328 --> 00:02:51.089
"That's Tosca," Joan said over the din.

55
00:02:51.109 --> 00:02:52.830
"She doesn't like dogs.

56
00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:57.211
I guess she suddenly realized there are a lot of them here.

57
00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:58.971
She got scared."

58
00:02:58.991 --> 00:03:02.204
"It's okay, Tosca," Daisy said.

59
00:03:02.224 --> 00:03:04.225
"You're safe in your cage."

60
00:03:05.445 --> 00:03:08.726
Yooowl! Tosca made even more noise!

61
00:03:11.727 --> 00:03:13.287
Daisy moved closer to her.

62
00:03:13.307 --> 00:03:16.628
"Please tell me what's wrong," she whispered.

63
00:03:16.648 --> 00:03:18.009
"Maybe I can help.

64
00:03:18.509 --> 00:03:20.069
I can understand animals."

65
00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:24.150
She repeated herself a few times.

66
00:03:24.931 --> 00:03:27.191
Finally Tosca stopped yowling.

67
00:03:27.211 --> 00:03:29.312
"Whew," Joan said.

68
00:03:30.012 --> 00:03:32.294
"Quick, let's get the dogs calmed down now."

69
00:03:33.054 --> 00:03:34.275
Daisy looked at Grace.

70
00:03:34.295 --> 00:03:39.118
"You should take Scamp away so he doesn't scare Tosca."

71
00:03:40.599 --> 00:03:45.222
As soon as Grace was gone, she said, "Sorry the dogs scared you, Tosca."

72
00:03:45.943 --> 00:03:47.644
"Huh?" Tosca said.

73
00:03:47.664 --> 00:03:49.785
"I don't like dogs.

74
00:03:50.606 --> 00:03:52.767
But I'm not scared of them."

75
00:03:52.787 --> 00:03:54.389
"You're not?"

76
00:03:54.729 --> 00:03:55.489
Daisy asked.

77
00:03:55.509 --> 00:03:56.790
"Then why—?"

78
00:03:57.351 --> 00:03:59.292
Beatrice buzzed around Daisy's head.

79
00:04:00.652 --> 00:04:05.194
"Quiet!" Just then Joan returned.

80
00:04:05.214 --> 00:04:08.495
"I'll move Tosca's cage so she can't see any dogs.

81
00:04:09.156 --> 00:04:10.816
But there's some great news.

82
00:04:11.577 --> 00:04:14.238
The commotion attracted lots of people to our booth.

83
00:04:14.938 --> 00:04:16.499
Some might want to adopt a pet."

84
00:04:17.659 --> 00:04:18.900
"That is great news."

85
00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:20.860
Daisy gave her a thumbs-up.

86
00:04:23.081 --> 00:04:25.122
The kids headed back toward the bandstand.

87
00:04:25.802 --> 00:04:29.124
Spike was singing a lively song, and people were dancing.

88
00:04:32.864 --> 00:04:35.307
The band finished and started another song.
